{"nodes": [{"id": "ai_openaihttp_test_retry_policy", "label": "One retry on 5xx/network, none on 4xx or abort", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "test/ai/openaiHttp.test.ts", "source_location": "L14-L78", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Shared PR-8 fault-tolerance policy used by both the streaming DM loop and the summarizer's one-shot call; the budget is bounded so a failing endpoint cannot loop."}, {"id": "ai_openaihttp_test_transient_vs_terminal_rate_limit", "label": "Transient upstream 429 retried; daily-quota/billing 429 is terminal", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "test/ai/openaiHttp.test.ts", "source_location": "L106-L185", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Free-tier reality: a shared upstream pool throttles for a few seconds, and an unretried 429 there cost a whole turn mid-scene in a live playtest. A daily-quota 429 is the opposite -- retrying only delays an error the player needs to see, so its body must stay readable."}, {"id": "ai_openaihttp_test_parse_retry_after", "label": "Retry-After parsed from seconds or HTTP-date, clamped", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "test/ai/openaiHttp.test.ts", "source_location": "L129-L153", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An absurd advertised wait (600s) clamps to 8s so a turn never hangs on the provider's say-so; nonsense and negative values return undefined, a past date returns 0."}], "edges": [{"source": "ai_openaihttp_test_retry_policy", "target": "ai_openaihttp_fetchwithretry", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "test/ai/openaiHttp.test.ts", "source_location": "L7", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "ai_openaihttp_test_retry_policy", "target": "ai_openaihttp_isaborterror", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "test/ai/openaiHt